          {
            "name": "Cloud tradecraft",
            "content": "NIGHT KESTREL obtains long-lived cloud access keys from public code repositories and CI logs, then calls GetCallerIdentity and ListBuckets from 203.0.113.9 within minutes of a key leaking. The actor copies object-storage data and launches GPU instances for cryptocurrency mining. Detection: alert on API calls from unfamiliar ASNs using long-lived keys, enforce short-lived credentials, and enable secret scanning in repositories."
